                                      ],
                       "description":  "When a runner is offline at a task\u0027s scheduled fire time, the catch-up reconciler decides what to do. Users select per-task behavior via the \u0027If the runner was down\u0027 selector, with three options that map to the runner\u0027s CatchUpPolicy enum: \u0027run_once\u0027 (default — collapse all missed slots into one execution after the runner returns), \u0027run\u0027 (execute each missed slot individually), and \u0027skip\u0027 (record each missed slot as MissedRunnerDown without executing). A \u0027Grace window\u0027 input sets the seconds of slack — slots within `now - grace` of restart are considered fresh and not eligible for catch-up. The selector is only relevant for time-based schedules (Cron / Once / Interval); condition-based schedules don\u0027t have missed slots.",
                       "precondition":  "New Task form is open and a time-based schedule (Cron / Once / Interval) is selected",
                       "provenance":  {
                                          "source":  "migrated"
                                      }
                   },
