                                                         },
                                              "source":  "migrated",
                                              "reviewed":  false,
                                              "enabled":  true
                                          }
                                      ],
                       "description":  "When a scheduled task\u0027s launch (start call) fails — e.g. workflow file missing, prompt-id not found, /prompts/run HTTP error, missing session_id — the runner increments task.consecutive_launch_failures and pushes next_run forward by min(base * 2^(failures-1), 86400) seconds. The task list surfaces this so the operator can see retries are being throttled. Required visual indicators: an orange \u0027launch_failed\u0027 badge on the task row, the next-run cell rendered as \u0027Next: in X (after N failures)\u0027 instead of plain \u0027Next: in X\u0027, and a tooltip explaining the wait. This is distinct from a runtime failure (status \u0027failed\u0027), which doesn\u0027t push next_run forward — backoff applies only to LaunchFailed.",
                       "precondition":  "At least one task in the list has consecutiveLaunchFailures \u003e 0",
                       "provenance":  {
                                          "source":  "migrated"
                                      }
                   },
